+| `framework/frameworks/base/0328-SableOS-older-code-loading-for-listed-apps-Pluto-TV.patch` | `f4ed08a03b518772ba77c3c0a1b4185fa1712c9b` + 0101-0327 | Android 14's read-only rule for loaded code (ENFORCE_READ_ONLY_JAVA_DCL, 218865702) is off for the apps listed in `persist.sys.sable.legacy_dcl` (comma-separated, `-` for none; `tv.pluto.android` until App Compatibility sets the list), so Pluto TV, whose ad library loads a jar it wrote to its cache, no longer crashes at start (owner report 2026-11-12). A user build refuses `am compat disable` for Play Store apps. Every other app keeps the rule; `SableCodeLoadingTest` checks the list. |
